<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Text Adventure</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%# Still one inline <style>: propshaft is here to serve JavaScript, and the
        reading experience is a stage of its own (`ta-api-iface`). Restyling
        anything is that task's job, not this file's. %>
    <style>
      :root { color-scheme: dark; }
      body {
        background: #14161a; color: #cfd3d8;
        font: 15px/1.6 ui-monospace, "DejaVu Sans Mono", monospace;
        margin: 0; padding: 2rem 1rem;
      }
      main { max-width: 44rem; margin: 0 auto; }
      h1 { font-size: 1.2rem; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #8ba0b4; }
      h2 { font-size: 1rem; color: #e6e9ec; margin: 0 0 .25rem; }
      a { color: #7fb2d8; }
      hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #262b31; margin: 1.5rem 0; }
      .preface { color: #9aa3ac; font-style: italic; white-space: pre-wrap; }
      .turn { white-space: pre-wrap; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }

      /* The log dims every turn but the newest, so a player who has scrolled
         can find where the turn they just took begins. Past turns take the
         preface's colour; the newest keeps full-strength body colour. Colour
         only -- the preface is italic as well, and a turn is not.
         `:last-of-type` is the marker: no class per entry, and on a brand new
         playthrough the opening scene is the only turn and so the newest one.
         While a turn is streaming the newest turn is the #stream div *below*
         the log, so the log carries `streaming` and nothing in it brightens.
         PlaythroughsControllerTest asserts these two selectors directly. */
      .log .turn { color: #9aa3ac; }
      .log:not(.streaming) > .turn:last-of-type { color: #cfd3d8; }
      .command { color: #d8c07f; margin: 0 0 .35rem; }
      .speaking { color: #8b939b; margin: 0 0 .35rem; }
      .place { color: #8b939b; margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
      .place strong { color: #cfd3d8; font-weight: normal; }
      .story { border: 1px solid #262b31; padding: .75rem 1rem; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
      .story p { color: #8b939b; margin: .25rem 0 .75rem; }
      form { display: flex; gap: .5rem; }
      input[type=text] {
        flex: 1; background: #0e1013; color: #cfd3d8; border: 1px solid #333b44;
        padding: .5rem .6rem; font: inherit;
      }
      button {
        background: #262b31; color: #cfd3d8; border: 1px solid #3a424b;
        padding: .5rem .9rem; font: inherit; cursor: pointer;
      }
      button:hover { background: #333b44; }
      .cursor::after { content: "\2588"; animation: blink 1s steps(2) infinite; }
      @keyframes blink { 50% { opacity: 0; } }
      .empty { color: #6b737b; }
      .alert { color: #d88f7f; border: 1px solid #4a3230; padding: .5rem .75rem; }

      /* The app talking rather than the world -- see Playthrough::SafetyNotice.
         Deliberately not `.alert`: nothing has gone wrong and the alarm colour
         would say it had. A left rule and the preface's grey put it plainly
         outside the fiction without shouting, and `.turn`'s pre-wrap is absent
         on purpose because this text is the app's own paragraphs rather than a
         model's. It sits at the foot of the log, where the turn would have
         been. */
      .notice {
        border-left: 2px solid #4a5a4a; padding: .1rem 0 .1rem .75rem;
        margin: 0 0 1.5rem; color: #9aa3ac;
      }
      .notice p { margin: .5rem 0; }
      .notice strong { color: #cfd3d8; font-weight: normal; }

      /* THE SLASH MENU -- what the play box can complete this turn with. It is
         a list under the input rather than an overlay: the input sits at the
         foot of the page, the log above it is what the player is reading, and a
         floating panel would cover the turn they just took. `.ask` is the
         positioning context and the only thing between the form and the page.

         Styled out of the pieces already here -- the input's own border and
         background, the log's dim grey for the hint -- so the menu reads as
         part of the box and not as a widget bolted to it. */
      .ask { position: relative; }
      .slash-menu {
        list-style: none; margin: .35rem 0 0; padding: 0;
        border: 1px solid #333b44; background: #0e1013; max-height: 12rem; overflow-y: auto;
      }
      .slash-option {
        padding: .25rem .6rem; cursor: pointer;
        display: flex; gap: .75rem; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between;
      }
      .slash-option[aria-selected="true"] { background: #262b31; color: #e6e9ec; }
      .slash-hint { color: #6b737b; font-size: 12px; }

      /* THE VERDICT ON A TURN -- the evaluation instrument, and the least
         styling that makes it usable without competing with the prose. The
         reading experience is still `ta-api-iface`'s job; this is not the
         restyling, it is one control kept out of the way of it.

         Barely visible until the row is hovered, because there is one of these
         under every turn in the log and the log is what the player is reading.
         The chosen verdict stays lit whether or not anything is hovered -- it
         is a record, not a hover state -- and each verdict keeps its own colour
         so a scrolled log can be scanned for the turns that were marked.

         `form` is flex and full-width in the rule above, which would put each
         of these on a line of its own; inline-flex is what keeps the whole
         control on one. */
      .verdict {
        display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem; align-items: center;
        margin: -1rem 0 1.5rem; opacity: .28; transition: opacity .12s;
      }
      .verdict:hover, .verdict:focus-within { opacity: 1; }
      .verdict:has(.chosen) { opacity: .85; }
      .verdict form { display: inline-flex; gap: .3rem; margin: 0; }
      .verdict input[type=submit], .verdict button {
        background: none; border: 1px solid #2b3238; color: #6b737b;
        padding: .05rem .4rem; font: inherit; font-size: 12px; cursor: pointer;
      }
      .verdict input[type=submit]:hover, .verdict button:hover { background: #1c2126; color: #cfd3d8; }
      .verdict .mark.chosen { border-color: currentColor; }
      .verdict .mark.good.chosen { color: #7fd8c0; }
      .verdict .mark.weak.chosen { color: #d8c07f; }
      .verdict .mark.bad.chosen { color: #d88f7f; }
      /* The note is a single line and sits beside the buttons rather than
         stretching to the width of the log. */
      .verdict .why input[type=text] {
        flex: 0 1 18rem; padding: .05rem .4rem; font-size: 12px; border-color: #2b3238;
      }
    </style>
    <%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <% if flash[:alert] %><p class="alert"><%= flash[:alert] %></p><% end %>
      <%= yield %>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
